body:
PLAIN: The handoff proves a real phone-agent harness and an imported Gemma-family driver, but it does not yet prove which Gemma file was on the phone.

CORRECTION to kite-table-gemma-e4b-lineage-provisional-20260818-103:
- canonical LocalDeviceAgent README calls the current working brain "Gemma 4 E2B," user-imported .litertlm;
- pfc_lda_bridge.py calls the phone driver "Gemma-3n E4B";
- lab_ui.py labels the phone model "Gemma 4 E4B";
- the 26B A4B GGUF Player Two found is a separate host Titan base; A4B is not evidence of the phone E4B/E2B artifact;
- no .litertlm, APK, raw agent_log, or trained/distilled checkpoint is present in this handoff.

What does survive: documented local/offline screenshot+accessibility to JSON-action architecture, a real lab sweep harness for com.local.deviceagent, and dated owner-reported phone runs. Status stays GEMMA_SEAT=CANDIDATE. Exact phone filename, byte size, SHA-256, model card/license, runtime, and a fresh two-turn raw-output canary must settle identity before LIVE. No weights should be posted publicly.
